<p>
Here's my process for preparing those intros with Emacs.
</p>

<p>
First, I create all the intro slides with LaTeX and TikZ using the function <code>emacsconf-stream-generate-in-between-pages</code> from <a href="https://git.emacsconf.org/emacsconf-el/tree/emacsconf-stream.el">emacsconf-stream.el</a>. This year, the template I'm using is <a href="https://sachachua.com/blog/2026/11/emacsconf-recording-and-re-recording-introductions/_template.tex">_template.tex</a> and the background image is <a href="https://sachachua.com/blog/2026/11/emacsconf-recording-and-re-recording-introductions/_template_bg.pdf">_template_bg.pdf</a>.
I used to use an SVG and just replace the elements within it (<a href="https://sachachua.com/blog/2026/11/emacsconf-recording-and-re-recording-introductions/template.svg">template.svg</a>, <a href="https://git.emacsconf.org/emacsconf-el/tree/emacsconf-stream.el">emacsconf-stream-generate-in-between-page-svg</a>). This year, some of the talk titles are very long and SVG doesn't have widespread support for wrapping.
LaTeX handles wrapping and positioning beautifully. This even allows me to have ligatures like the "ff" in Jeff Trull's name.
I noticed those ligatures disappeared when I used Inkscape to convert to PNG, so I needed this command instead:
<code>inkscape &#45;&#45;pdf-poppler &#45;&#45;export-type=png -w 1280 -h 720 &#45;&#45;export-background-opacity=0 &#45;&#45;export-text-to-path</code>
</p>

<p>
This is the function that generates the individual intro slide:
</p>

<p>
</p><details><summary>emacsconf-stream-generate-in-between-page: Use LaTeX to generate the intro slide for TALK based on assets/in-between/_template.tex.</summary><div class="org-src-container"><pre class="src src-emacs-lisp">(<span class="org-keyword">defun</span> <span class="org-function-name">emacsconf-stream-generate-in-between-page</span> (talk <span class="org-type">&amp;optional</span> prev info force)
  <span class="org-doc">"Use LaTeX to generate the intro slide for TALK based on assets/in-between/_template.tex."</span>
  (<span class="org-keyword">interactive</span> (list (emacsconf-complete-talk-info)))
  (<span class="org-keyword">let*</span> ((prev (<span class="org-keyword">or</span> prev (emacsconf-previous-talk talk info)))
         (dir (expand-file-name <span class="org-string">"in-between"</span> emacsconf-stream-asset-dir))
         (template
          (<span class="org-keyword">with-temp-buffer</span>
            (insert-file-contents
             (expand-file-name <span class="org-string">"_template.tex"</span> dir))
            (buffer-string)))
         (default-directory dir))
    (write-region
     (emacsconf-replace-plist-in-string
      (list
       <span class="org-builtin">:current-title</span>
       (<span class="org-keyword">or</span> (plist-get talk <span class="org-builtin">:title</span>) <span class="org-string">""</span>)
       <span class="org-builtin">:current-speakers</span>
       (<span class="org-keyword">or</span> (plist-get talk <span class="org-builtin">:speakers</span>) <span class="org-string">""</span>)
       <span class="org-builtin">:current-details</span>
       (format <span class="org-string">"%s\\\\\n%s"</span>
               (<span class="org-keyword">or</span> (plist-get talk <span class="org-builtin">:absolute-url</span>) <span class="org-string">""</span>)
               (<span class="org-keyword">pcase</span> (plist-get talk <span class="org-builtin">:q-and-a</span>)
                 ((<span class="org-keyword">rx</span> <span class="org-string">"live"</span>) <span class="org-string">"Live Q\\&amp;A after talk"</span>)
                 ((<span class="org-keyword">rx</span> <span class="org-string">"pad"</span>) <span class="org-string">"Etherpad"</span>)
                 ((<span class="org-keyword">rx</span> <span class="org-string">"IRC"</span>) <span class="org-string">"IRC Q\\&amp;A after talk"</span>)
                 (_ <span class="org-string">""</span>)))
       <span class="org-builtin">:previous-title</span>
       (<span class="org-keyword">or</span> (plist-get prev <span class="org-builtin">:title</span>) <span class="org-string">""</span>)
       <span class="org-builtin">:conf-name</span> emacsconf-name
       <span class="org-builtin">:conf-year</span> emacsconf-year
       <span class="org-builtin">:previous-speakers</span>
       (<span class="org-keyword">or</span> (plist-get prev <span class="org-builtin">:speakers</span>) <span class="org-string">""</span>)
       <span class="org-builtin">:previous-details</span>
       (format <span class="org-string">"%s\\\\\n%s"</span>
               (<span class="org-keyword">or</span> (plist-get prev <span class="org-builtin">:absolute-url</span>) <span class="org-string">""</span>)
               (<span class="org-keyword">pcase</span> (plist-get prev <span class="org-builtin">:q-and-a</span>)
                 ((<span class="org-keyword">rx</span> <span class="org-string">"live"</span>) <span class="org-string">"Live Q\\&amp;A after talk"</span>)
                 ((<span class="org-keyword">rx</span> <span class="org-string">"pad"</span>) <span class="org-string">"Etherpad"</span>)
                 ((<span class="org-keyword">rx</span> <span class="org-string">"IRC"</span>) <span class="org-string">"IRC Q\\&amp;A after talk"</span>)
                 (_ <span class="org-string">""</span>))))
      template)
     nil
     (expand-file-name (concat (plist-get talk <span class="org-builtin">:slug</span>) <span class="org-string">".tex"</span>) dir))
    (shell-command
     (format <span class="org-string">"lualatex -shell-escape %s &amp;&amp; inkscape &#45;&#45;pdf-poppler &#45;&#45;export-type=png -w 1280 -h 720 &#45;&#45;export-background-opacity=0 &#45;&#45;export-text-to-path %s"</span>
             (expand-file-name (concat (plist-get talk <span class="org-builtin">:slug</span>) <span class="org-string">".tex"</span>)
                               dir)
             (expand-file-name (concat (plist-get talk <span class="org-builtin">:slug</span>) <span class="org-string">".pdf"</span>)
                               dir)))))

</pre></div></details>
